<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xiao Yanyan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">953–<a href="/years/1009">1009</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Empress Dowager Chengtian, Xiao Chuo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Xiao Yanyan, known as Empress Dowager Chengtian, was the widow of Emperor Jingzong of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> and regent for her son Shengzong from 982 until her death in 1009. A capable ruler and military commander, she reformed the government and in 1004 led the campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> that ended in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanyuan-treaty">Chanyuan Treaty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xiao-yanyan.jpg" alt="Xiao Yanyan" width="220" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 熊大木 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empress_Dowager_Xiao_1892.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
